    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2212.12579v2</id>
    <title>Abelian Sandpiles on Cylinders</title>
    <updated>2023-02-20T08:34:29Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.12579v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2212.12579v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We study here a variant of the Abelian Sandpile Model, where the playground is a cylinder of width $w$ and of circumference c. When c &lt;&lt; w, we describe a phenomenon which has not been observed in other geometries: the probability distribution of avalanche sizes has a ladder structure, with the first step consisting of avalanches of size up to w c/2 that are essentially equiprobable, except for a small exponential tail of order about 10c. We explain this phenomenon and describe subsequent steps.</summary>
